      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hidden costs often manifest as \"load fees\" in mutual funds, which are upfront or sales charges that eat directly into initial investment returns. For ETFs, unexpected costs can include trading commissions if you buy or sell through a brokerage with fees, or tracking error if the active management of a passive ETF fails to perfectly mimic its index. These fees collectively reduce the net return, causing the actual portfolio performance to lag behind the stated fund goals.",
